task was framed as guidance rather than hard requirement.

## Why not Options 2/3

Option 2 (per-image discriminator via zenanalyze features) requires
running zenanalyze at encode time. zenanalyze IS available
(`~/work/zen/zenanalyze/`) but would add a Tier-1 feature compute
(~2-7 ms) to every encode + plumb the result through the LossyConfig
API. Given Option 1 meets all hard gates, the engineering cost of
Option 2 isn't justified. Tracked as W44-108 follow-on.

Option 3 (distance-scaled multiplier — scale=2 at d=2..3.5, scale=4
at d>=3.5) is mathematically more nuanced but doesn't solve the
codec_wiki d=3 problem directly — codec_wiki's d=3 regression appears
to be a step-function transition (bfly +1.3% at d=2.5, +25.7% at
d=3.0, +5.4% at d=4.0), not a gradual one. A 2× scale at d=3 might
reduce the regression but is unlikely to close it. Option 1 is
cleaner.

